# 📘 Lesson 11 — SOLID Principles

> [!TIP]
> **SOLID** is a set of five principles that help us write code that is **maintainable, flexible, testable, and loosely coupled**.

---

## 🧠 SOLID at a Glance

> [!NOTE]
>
> ### Remember **SOLID**
>
> **S** → **Single Responsibility** → One responsibility / one reason to change
> **O** → **Open/Closed** → Open for extension, closed for modification
> **L** → **Liskov Substitution** → Child should safely replace parent
> **I** → **Interface Segregation** → Don't force classes to depend on things they don't need
> **D** → **Dependency Inversion** → Depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations

|    Principle   | Simple Meaning                         |
| :------------: | -------------------------------------- |
| 🟢 **S — SRP** | One responsibility                     |
| 🔵 **O — OCP** | Extend without modifying existing code |
| 🟣 **L — LSP** | Child should safely replace parent     |
| 🟠 **I — ISP** | Keep interfaces small and focused      |
| 🔴 **D — DIP** | Depend on abstractions                 |

---

# 1. 🟢 S — Single Responsibility Principle

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **A class should have one clear responsibility and one reason to change.**

The goal of SRP is to avoid putting unrelated responsibilities inside a single class.

### ❌ Bad Example

```csharp
public class Employee
{
    public void CalculateSalary()
    {
        // Salary calculation
    }

    public void SaveToDatabase()
    {
        // Database logic
    }

    public void SendEmail()
    {
        // Email logic
    }
}
```

The `Employee` class now has **three different responsibilities**:

* Calculate salary
* Save to database
* Send email

That means it has multiple reasons to change.

### ✅ Better Example

```csharp
public class SalaryCalculator
{
    public decimal CalculateSalary()
    {
        return 50000;
    }
}

public class EmployeeRepository
{
    public void Save()
    {
        // Database logic
    }
}

public class EmailService
{
    public void SendEmail()
    {
        // Email logic
    }
}
```

> [!TIP]
>
> ### 🧠 Mental Model
>
> **One Class → One Responsibility → One Reason to Change**

---

# 2. 🔵 O — Open/Closed Principle

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Software entities should be open for extension but closed for modification.**

### Open for Extension

We should be able to **add new behavior**.

### Closed for Modification

We should not have to keep modifying stable existing code whenever we add new behavior.

---

## 💰 Example — Discount System

### ❌ Without OCP

```csharp
public decimal CalculateDiscount(
    string customerType,
    decimal amount)
{
    if (customerType == "Regular")
    {
        return amount * 0.05m;
    }
    else if (customerType == "Premium")
    {
        return amount * 0.10m;
    }
    else if (customerType == "VIP")
    {
        return amount * 0.20m;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

> [!WARNING]
> Every time we add a new discount type, we have to **modify existing code**.

---

### ✅ Using OCP

Create an abstraction:

```csharp
public interface IDiscountStrategy
{
    decimal Calculate(decimal amount);
}
```

Implement different strategies:

```csharp
public class RegularDiscount : IDiscountStrategy
{
    public decimal Calculate(decimal amount)
    {
        return amount * 0.05m;
    }
}

public class PremiumDiscount : IDiscountStrategy
{
    public decimal Calculate(decimal amount)
    {
        return amount * 0.10m;
    }
}

public class VIPDiscount : IDiscountStrategy
{
    public decimal Calculate(decimal amount)
    {
        return amount * 0.20m;
    }
}
```

Need another discount?

```csharp
public class EmployeeDiscount : IDiscountStrategy
{
    public decimal Calculate(decimal amount)
    {
        return amount * 0.30m;
    }
}
```

No existing discount class needs to be modified.

### 🧠 Mental Model

```text
                 IDiscountStrategy
                        │
          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
          ↓             ↓             ↓
       Regular       Premium          VIP
         5%            10%            20%
                                     
                        +
                        
                   Employee
                     30%
```

> [!TIP]
> **OCP = Add new behavior without modifying stable existing behavior.**

